      {
        "id": 70548,
        "name": "dwetuski",
        "username": "dwetuski",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/3e96dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-12T17:39:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Damage delt is always a result of HP loss though.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That can't be right. &nbsp;If this were true, a target would have to actually lose hp before Divine Sacrifice or Wrest the Mind could redirect damage away from it.</p>\n<p>Could it be that you're thinking of the fact that a target doesn't \"take damage\" if the target is immune to the type of damage it's dealt of if the damage it's dealt is reduced below 1? &nbsp;I think that \"takes damage\" is a distinct concept from \"deals damage\".</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:49:26.912Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
