      {
        "id": 70550,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-12T18:11:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><span>Generally, if a source dealt damage, it reduced HP. If no HP was lost, no damage was dealt.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Maybe this might be a better way to pose it and alter your steps.</p><p>1) Damage sequence declared. Determine target/base damage/type/source</p><p>2) Evaluate all damage modifiers</p><p><span>3) Damage is dealt</span></p><p><span>3a) \"Would be dealt damage\" triggers and effects take place. If redirection was used, start from step 1 with new target</span></p><p>3b) \"When target deals/is dealt\" damage triggers and effects take place.&nbsp;<span>If redirection was used, start from step 1 with new target</span></p><p>4) Reduce HP</p><p>4a) \"Target dealt damage this way\" triggers and effects</p><p>Edit: Modified this a bit</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:49:27.063Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
