      {
        "id": 70551,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-13T03:55:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Just to stress this point:</p><p>Bunker's incap ability is not Damage Reduction. &nbsp;It prevents damage and works against irreducible damage. &nbsp;It works like a limited immunity, basically the target is immune to the first two points of damage, except that it is Bunker preventing the damage.</p><blockquote><p>So, here's how I think the order should be:</p><p>1) Damage is declared, which constitutes determining the original amount, type, source, and target of the damage.</p><p>2) Damage increases/reductions that affect damage dealt by a source are applied.</p><p>3) Damage \"is dealt\" by the source, at which point one or more of the 2 redirect effects might modify the target.</p><p>4) Damage \"would be dealt\" to the target, at which point one or more of the 8 redirect effects might modify the target.</p><p>5) Immunity may cancel the damage entirely, ending the sequence immediately.</p><p>6) Damage increases/reductions that affect damage dealt to a target are applied.</p><p>7) The target's hp is reduced.</p></blockquote><p>Good job with the card survey, the only two that don't have would be dealt are dealing with effects that don't care about the target, sacrifice is source based (targets fanatic damaged have their damage redirected), just like Wrest the Mind.</p><p>As for the timing above, I would put all \"Would be dealt\" effects in theStep 4 as they are all triggered then. &nbsp;That might be your intent but it looks like you could just mean redirects there. &nbsp;At the point where those trigger I think the group playing the game should decide what happens. &nbsp;If you can keep track of all the card orders and want to do it that way, go for it, if your group doesn't want to track card order across four heroes and villain cards too, then let the heroes decide. &nbsp;I've never been able to keep what cards were played first in my head (even laying them out in order I still don't know because cards from different play areas trigger at the same time, and keeping that straight is like work).</p><p>The immunity timing is wrong, I believe it is official (it is in Spiffs PDF) that a target immune to damage cannot redirect it. &nbsp;I just checked today as I thought about this some more. &nbsp;So I'd time it up like this:</p><p>1: &nbsp;Damage Declaration, initial Source, type, amount and target are declared.</p><p>2: &nbsp;Apply changes to damage type.</p><p>3: &nbsp;Apply modifiers to damage based on source and type.</p><p>4: &nbsp;Source of damage steps complete, check for redirection based on source, proceed to target.</p><p>5. &nbsp;If target is immune end damage calculations, no damage is dealt.</p><p>6. &nbsp;Trigger all \"would be dealt damage\" reduction and redirection effects.</p><p>7. &nbsp;Trigger all \"is dealt damage\" modifiers.</p><p>8, &nbsp;Reduce targets HP.</p><p>Unless Spiff's PDF is wrong (I doubt) or has been superceeded step 5 needs to be there.</p><p>This list is going to change how I play, I can't use WtM to steer damage Iron Legacy redirects back at him, which makes a lot of sense thematically.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
