      {
        "id": 70552,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-13T04:03:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Just to stress this point:Haka's incap ability is not Damage Reduction. &nbsp;It prevents damage and works against irreducible damage. &nbsp;It works like a limited immunity, basically the target is immune to the first two points of damage, except that it is Haka preventing the damage</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Haka's incap side is \"Select a Hero. Decrease the next damage to that hero by 2\" i'm not sure how you are getting prevention from it. It looks to me that it may be the case of inconsistant wording, and should be \"reduce the next damage to that hero by 2\".</p>",
